{"path":"s37","heading":"Appealable orders.","in_1996":true,"nodes_1996":[{"path":"s37","node_type":"section","number":"37","heading":"Appealable orders.","text":""},{"path":"s37.ss1","node_type":"subsection","number":"1","heading":null,"text":"An appeal shall lie from the following orders (and from no others) to the Court authorised by law to hear appeals from original decrees of the Court passing the order, namely:—"},{"path":"s37.ss1.cl(a)","node_type":"clause","number":"a","heading":null,"text":"granting or refusing to grant any measure under section 9;"},{"path":"s37.ss1.cl(b)","node_type":"clause","number":"b","heading":null,"text":"setting aside or refusing to set aside an arbitral award under section 34."},{"path":"s37.ss2","node_type":"subsection","number":"2","heading":null,"text":"Appeal shall also lie to a court from an order of the arbitral tribunal—"},{"path":"s37.ss2.cl(a)","node_type":"clause","number":"a","heading":null,"text":"accepting the plea referred to in sub-section (2) or sub-section (3) of section 16; or"},{"path":"s37.ss2.cl(b)","node_type":"clause","number":"b","heading":null,"text":"granting or refusing to grant an interim measure under section 17."},{"path":"s37.ss3","node_type":"subsection","number":"3","heading":null,"text":"No second appeal shall lie from an order passed in appeal under this section, but nothing in this section shall affect or take away any right to appeal to the Supreme Court."}],"events":[{"instrument":"3/2016","title":"Arbitration and Conciliation (Amendment) Act, 2015 (No. 3 of 2016)","effective":"from 23 Oct 2015 (Ordinance 9 of 2015)","edges":[{"instrument":"3/2016","old":null,"new":"s37.ss1.cl(a)","op_type":"insert","source":"agent","group":"3/2016|s20","confidence":0.99,"rationale":"Clause (a) introduces a new ground not present in the old provision, so it is an insertion."},{"instrument":"3/2016","old":"s37.ss1.cl(a)","new":"s37.ss1.cl(b)","op_type":"renumber","source":"agent","group":"3/2016|s20","confidence":0.99,"rationale":"The text of new clause (b) is identical to the old clause (a), thus it is the same provision moved to a new label."},{"instrument":"3/2016","old":"s37.ss1.cl(b)","new":"s37.ss1.cl(c)","op_type":"renumber","source":"agent","group":"3/2016|s20","confidence":0.99,"rationale":"The text of new clause (c) matches the old clause (b), so it is a renumbering of that provision."}],"instructions":{"3/2016|s20":"In section 37 of the principal Act, in sub-section (1), for clauses (a) and (b), the following clauses shall be substituted, namely:— “(a) refusing to refer the parties to arbitration under section 8; (b) granting or refusing to grant any measure under section 9; (c) setting aside or refusing to set aside an arbitral award under section 34.”."},"intent":[{"unit":"3/2016|s20","status":"sourced","claim":"The amendments seek to make disposal of commercial disputes more user-friendly and cost effective, which, in turn, will lead to expeditious disposal of cases.","tier":"debate","quote":"The amendments seek to make disposal of commercial disputes more user-friendly and cost effective, which, in turn, will lead to expeditious\ndisposal of cases.","document_id":39,"span":[67341,67499],"attribution":{"by":"SHRI THOTA NARASIMHAM (KAKINADA)","role":"member","where":"Lok Sabha debate, 17 Dec 2015: further discussion on the Statutory Resolution disapproving Ordinance 9 of 2015 and the Arbitration and Conciliation (Amendment) Bill, 2015 (Bill passed)"},"tiers_searched":["sor","debate"]}]},{"instrument":"33/2019","title":"Arbitration and Conciliation (Amendment) Act, 2019 (No. 33 of 2019)","effective":"in part: ss. 1, 4–9, 11–13, 15 from 30 Aug 2019 (S.O. 3154(E)); other sections by later notification or not commenced","edges":[{"instrument":"33/2019","old":"s37.ss1","new":"s37.ss1","op_type":"substitute","source":"rule","group":"33/2019|s8","confidence":1.0,"rationale":null}],"instructions":{"33/2019|s8":"In section 37 of the principal Act, in sub-section (1), 